# Git-crypt encrypted files.
#
# Files matching the patterns below are encrypted on commit (clean filter)
# and decrypted on checkout (smudge filter) using the symmetric key in
# `pass show git/crypt-key`. Filter is wired by `shell/.local/bin/git-crypt`,
# invoked automatically by `shell/.postinstall` after a fresh clone.
#
# To activate manually: cd ~/.dotfiles && ./shell/.local/bin/git-crypt init
#
# Until activated, the patterns below are no-ops — git's filter resolution
# falls through to identity when filter.git-crypt.* is unset, so adding
# this file to a fresh clone is harmless.

*.env filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt
